## Architecture & Design Principles

### 1. Cloud-Native Architecture

**Core Principle:**
Veeva is built on cloud-native architecture designed for scalability, availability, and security.

**Key Characteristics:**
```
Scalability:
├─ Horizontal scaling: Add capacity without downtime
├─ Elastic infrastructure: Auto-scale based on demand
├─ Multi-tenant: Efficient resource sharing across customers
└─ Geographic distribution: Data centers worldwide

Availability:
├─ 99.9% uptime SLA (99.99% for Enterprise)
├─ Redundancy: Data replicated across zones
├─ Failover: Automatic in case of failure
└─ Load balancing: Distribute traffic across servers

Security:
├─ Defense in depth: Multiple security layers
├─ End-to-end encryption: Data in transit & at rest
├─ Zero trust: Verify every access request
└─ Compliance: SOC 2, ISO 27001, HIPAA-ready
```

### 2. Microservices Architecture

**Concept:**
Veeva decomposes functionality into independent microservices that communicate via APIs.

**Benefits:**
```
✓ Independent scaling: Only scale services under load
✓ Technology flexibility: Each service uses best-fit tech
✓ Rapid deployment: Update services independently
✓ Fault isolation: One service failure doesn't crash all
✓ Team autonomy: Teams own specific services

Services in Veeva:
├─ Authentication Service
├─ Document Management Service
├─ Workflow Engine
├─ Search & Indexing Service
├─ Notification Service
├─ Audit & Compliance Service
├─ Integration Service
└─ Analytics Service
```

### 3. Event-Driven Architecture

**Pattern:**
Services communicate asynchronously through events, decoupling producers from consumers.

**Example - Document Published Event:**
```
Document Service publishes: "document.published"
├─ Notification Service: Sends email to stakeholders
├─ Search Service: Indexes document for searching
├─ Analytics Service: Records publication event
├─ Archive Service: Creates backup
└─ Integration Service: Notifies external systems

Advantages:
✓ Loose coupling: Services don't directly depend
✓ Scalability: Each service scales independently
✓ Resilience: If one fails, others continue
✓ Extensibility: Add new consumers without modifying originals
```

### 4. API-First Design

**Principle:**
All functionality exposed through APIs; UI built on top of APIs.

**Benefits:**
```
API-First Approach:

Platform Level:
├─ Vault APIs → CRUD operations on documents
├─ CRM APIs → Account, call, territory management
├─ CLM APIs → Content distribution and tracking
└─ Integration APIs → Webhooks, queues, listeners

UI Level:
├─ Web UI: Built with REST/GraphQL calls
├─ Mobile App: Same APIs as web
├─ Third-party integrations: Access same APIs
└─ Custom solutions: Build on same foundation

This ensures:
✓ Consistency across all interfaces
✓ Easy to build new solutions
✓ No "hidden" features only in UI
✓ Automation possible for any operation
```

